version of the aforementioned "think step by step" prompt modification.</sp=
an></p><p>Note that this involves supervised finetuning (SFT) to generate t=
he initial model, so it's not a pure inference-time scaling approach. Howev=
er, the end goal is actively controlling the reasoning behavior through inf=
erence-time scaling; hence, I considered this paper for the "1. Inference-t=
ime compute scaling" category.</p><p>In short, their approach is twofold:</=
p><ol><li><p>Create a curated SFT dataset with 1k training examples that in=
clude reasoning traces.</p></li><li><p>Control the length of responses by:<=
/p></li><li><p>a) Appending "Wait" tokens to get the LLM to generate longer=
 responses, self-verify, and correct itself, or</p></li><li><p>b) Stopping =
generation by adding an end-of-thinking token delimiter ("Final Answer:"). =
They call this length control "budget forcing."</p></li></ol><div class=3D"=
